course: dictionary
lesson: 13663
title: Short words: info
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Info» is a short form of «information», and it means facts or details about something. People use it in casual talk, texts and on signs, so it helps to know it when you read quickly.
explain: «Can you send me more info about the trip?» Here info means the details, such as where, when and how much. If you swap in the full word, «Can you send me more information about the trip?», the sentence still makes sense, so you know the meaning is right.
explain: On a sign or a button, info means "information here". «Go to the info desk» means go to the place where you can get details. «Press the info button» means press it to see more.
explain: Info is a casual word. In formal writing, such as a letter to your head teacher, use «information» instead.
fact: Info is an informal short form of information.
fact: Info means facts or details about something.
fact: On signs and buttons, info means "information here", as in «info desk».
fact: «Contact info» means the details you need to get in touch, such as a phone number or email.
fact: «FYI» stands for «for your info», a casual way to say "I am telling you this so you know."
exercise: «Got any info on the trip?» What does info mean here? | *Details about the trip | A new trip | A type of bus | A fast train
exercise: Which sign would help you find the place where you can get details? | Exit | Lost property | Toilets | *Info desk
exercise: Ruby is writing a formal letter to her head teacher. Which word should she use instead of info? | info-ish | details-bit | *information | infos
test: «More info is on the sheet.» What does more info mean? | *More details | More games | More rain | More food
test: Which phrase means the details you need to get in touch with someone? | Info button | *Contact info | Info desk | For your info
exam: What does «FYI» in a text mean? | *For your information | Fast yes, I agree | Fix your iPad | Fine, you're invited
